# The upstream builders are VENDORED here (no runtime fetch). This file records
# exactly which channel-rootfs state each vendored tree corresponds to.
# To move to a newer channel-rootfs state: replace the trees manually and
# update the SHAs below. Firmware is NOT vendored: the vendored rootfs recipes
# clone the GitLab channel-firmware repo at build time; a local tree can be
# used offline via FIRMWARE_SOURCE_DIR.
# Upstream itself now carries the lean shape (zero validations, no logs, conf
# API). The vendored copies additionally mirror the LOCAL two-layer split:
# the kernel make/pack stage (sh/build.sh) is param-driven and the local
# orchestrator (sh/mainline/build.sh, sh/rootfs/build.sh) owns sources,
# cache and build layout, with the raw-ext4 generator in sh/lib/.
